{
  "version": "2.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Workspace as Recursive Graph Document",
    "kind": "idea",
    "version": "0.2.0",
    "preferredViewer": "https://twilite.zone"
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "declaration",
      "type": "declaration",
      "label": "Workspace as Recursive Graph Document",
      "position": {
        "x": -620,
        "y": -520
      },
      "width": 430,
      "height": 270,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "recursive-workspace-document",
          "nodeId": "recursive-workspace-document",
          "name": "Workspace as Recursive Graph Document",
          "version": "0.2.0",
          "description": "An Idea graph for saving a Twilite workspace as an ordinary .node graph containing Portal-backed projections of exposed nodes, parent-owned edges, and graph-level machinery."
        },
        "intent": {
          "kind": "idea",
          "scope": "local",
          "status": "proposal"
        },
        "document": {
          "url": "github://twilite-zone/public/ideas/recursive-workspace-document/root.node"
        },
        "declaration": {
          "kind": "idea",
          "targetMode": "artifact",
          "defaultSurfaceId": "",
          "surfaces": []
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "idea",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "The idea",
      "position": {
        "x": -100,
        "y": -520
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 300,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#2a1d3b",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#ad7aff",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 18
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Idea \u00b7 workspace is a graph\n\nSave a workspace as an ordinary `.node` document. The workspace owns Portal-backed instances of nodes exposed by other documents, their spatial arrangement, ordinary parent-level edges, and all graph machinery authored at that level.\n\nChild documents remain separate authorities. Their contents are resolved when needed, never copied into the workspace file."
      },
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "problem",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Boundary we have reached",
      "position": {
        "x": 500,
        "y": -520
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 300,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#172033",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#52627d",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 18
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Problem\n\nThe runtime workspace can arrange graphs and own typed edges, but it is not yet a complete graph-level authority. Consequently its edge classes do not have a proper Legend, its arrangement lives in session storage, and its Views, Ports, Portals, and Bridges have no durable containing document."
      },
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "recursive-rule",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Recursive rule",
      "position": {
        "x": -1080,
        "y": -120
      },
      "width": 500,
      "height": 310,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#17302c",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#49c7a5",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 18
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Proposed invariant\n\nEvery `.node` document saves only the structure authored at its own level. A child document exposes a semantic node through a Port; the parent stores a Portal-backed instance that resolves that exposure and renders one of the node's Views. Unfolding does not transfer ownership of the child document.\n\nThe same Declaration \u2192 View \u2192 Port \u2192 Portal \u2192 Bridge \u2192 Edge vocabulary applies at every level. No new `graph` node primitive is required."
      },
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "workspace-owns",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "The workspace document owns",
      "position": {
        "x": -520,
        "y": -120
      },
      "width": 500,
      "height": 360,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#17302c",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#49c7a5",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 18
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Authored in the workspace\n\n- its Declaration and identity\n- Portal-backed instances targeting exposed nodes\n- placement, size, labels, and groups for those instances\n- ordinary edges between the resolved node instances\n- edge-class references and Legend configuration\n- workspace Views and exposed Ports\n- workspace Portals and unbound export capabilities\n- any ordinary content authored in the workspace\n\nThese are normal graph data, not a parallel workspace schema."
      },
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "child-owns",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Referenced graphs retain",
      "position": {
        "x": 40,
        "y": -120
      },
      "width": 500,
      "height": 360,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#17302c",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#49c7a5",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 18
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Authored in each child document\n\n- the child Declaration and document authority\n- semantic node identity\n- Views and selectable surfaces\n- Ports that expose the node and its surfaces\n- child-local Portals, nodes, and edges\n- unbound capabilities intentionally published by that node\n\nThe workspace stores a document ref plus the exposed Port it consumes. The Port resolves the node and permitted View; the workspace does not serialize the loaded child snapshot."
      },
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "derived",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Recompute, do not save",
      "position": {
        "x": 600,
        "y": -120
      },
      "width": 500,
      "height": 360,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#302717",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#e2b45d",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 18
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Derived presentation\n\n- export/import Bridge projections produced by a parent edge\n- boundary apertures and crossing geometry\n- reduced-detail graph presentations\n- shared-surface projections\n- loaded child snapshots and caches\n- dirty, loading, access, selection, focus, and active state\n\nDerived structures may look like nodes, but their authority remains the authored structure from which they were extrapolated."
      },
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "reference-shape",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Portal-backed node instance",
      "position": {
        "x": -1080,
        "y": 330
      },
      "width": 500,
      "height": 390,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#172033",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#52627d",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 18
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Candidate instance shape\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"customer-placement\",\n  \"type\": \"portal\",\n  \"position\": { \"x\": 800, \"y\": 240 },\n  \"width\": 900,\n  \"height\": 640,\n  \"data\": {\n    \"target\": {\n      \"kind\": \"node\",\n      \"ref\": \"github://owner/repo/customers/root.node\",\n      \"portId\": \"customer-summary\",\n      \"surfaceId\": \"summary\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe local `id` identifies this placement. `ref` locates document authority; the exposed Port resolves semantic `nodeId` and the permitted View. Resolved fields need not be redundantly authored."
      },
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "views",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Views across levels",
      "position": {
        "x": -520,
        "y": 330
      },
      "width": 500,
      "height": 390,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#172033",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#52627d",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 18
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# View extrapolation\n\nA child document owns the `summary`, `detail`, icon, or other Views of its semantic node. Its exposed Port selects or permits those surfaces. A Portal-backed parent instance consumes that exposure. At a distant scale the selected View represents the node; zooming closer may reveal more child structure.\n\nThe workspace can independently own Views of its whole arrangement. No child View is copied into the parent."
      },
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "edges",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Edges and Bridges",
      "position": {
        "x": 40,
        "y": 330
      },
      "width": 500,
      "height": 390,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#172033",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#52627d",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 18
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Parent edge is authoritative\n\nAn edge between resolved node instances is an ordinary edge in the workspace document. Its edge class belongs in the workspace Legend. The endpoints are parent-local instance IDs whose Portal targets preserve child provenance and semantic identity.\n\nWhen an endpoint unfolds, Twilite derives export and import Bridge projections carrying the parent edge ID. An explicitly authored unbound export Bridge remains a capability until a parent edge is created."
      },
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "load-save",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Load and save lifecycle",
      "position": {
        "x": 600,
        "y": 330
      },
      "width": 500,
      "height": 390,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#172033",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#52627d",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 18
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Lifecycle\n\n1. Load the workspace document.\n2. Render its local Portal-backed instances from durable placement data.\n3. Resolve each target document's exposed Port, semantic node, and required View.\n4. Unfold a child without changing the parent document.\n5. Author parent-level gestures into the workspace graph.\n6. Save the workspace as ordinary graph JSON.\n7. Save dirty child documents separately through Save All."
      },
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "identity-question",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Open identity question",
      "position": {
        "x": -1080,
        "y": 800
      },
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#332033",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#ef8ee5",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 18
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Question \u00b7 repeated projections\n\nCan one workspace contain several local instances consuming the same exposed Port?\n\n**Proposal:** yes. Each placement has a graph-local `id`; all may resolve the same document, Port, semantic `nodeId`, and View. Placement identity must not be confused with referenced semantic identity."
      },
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "camera-question",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Open presentation question",
      "position": {
        "x": -520,
        "y": 800
      },
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#332033",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#ef8ee5",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 18
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Question \u00b7 camera and named arrangements\n\nShould the current camera be saved?\n\n**Proposal:** focus and transient camera remain session state. Portable named presentations should be authored as ordinary workspace Views. A default View may establish an intentional opening camera without serializing incidental navigation."
      },
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cycle-risk",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Risk \u00b7 recursive loading",
      "position": {
        "x": 40,
        "y": 800
      },
      "width": 500,
      "height": 300,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#3a2222",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#f27d7d",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 18
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Risk \u00b7 cycles and load cost\n\nWorkspace A may reference B while B eventually references A. Reference resolution must therefore be lazy, bounded, and cycle-aware. Saving must never expand references into embedded snapshots, or a small cyclic composition could become unbounded."
      },
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "implementation",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Proposed implementation slices",
      "position": {
        "x": 600,
        "y": 800
      },
      "width": 500,
      "height": 390,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#202a3d",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#78a6ff",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 18
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Implementation path\n\n1. Define durable Portal-backed instance serialization for exposed nodes.\n2. Convert runtime workspace instances into those ordinary parent graph nodes.\n3. Resolve `ref` \u2192 Port \u2192 semantic node \u2192 View without introducing a `graph` node type.\n4. Serialize workspace-owned edges as ordinary edges.\n5. Build a workspace Legend from its edge classes and capabilities.\n6. Load the workspace `.node` into the existing multi-document runtime.\n7. Keep child saves independent and migrate existing local-storage arrangements.\n8. Exercise recursive View, Port, Portal, Bridge, and edge behavior with smoke graphs.\n\nThis is an attempted solution for review, not a frozen contract."
      },
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "acceptance",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Review checkpoint",
      "position": {
        "x": -240,
        "y": 1260
      },
      "width": 720,
      "height": 350,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#1e2f23",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#7ed69b",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 18
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# What would make this convincing?\n\n- Opening one workspace file reconstructs the arrangement from Portal targets and exposed Ports.\n- The file contains no child nodes, child edges, or cached snapshots.\n- Every rendered child instance resolves a semantic node and one of its exposed Views.\n- `smoke-signal` appears in the workspace-level Legend.\n- Dragging fixture 10's export capability creates an ordinary workspace edge.\n- Unfolding either endpoint derives the same edge through Bridge projections.\n- Child graphs remain clean until directly edited.\n- A workspace can expose one of its own nodes through a Port, allowing another graph to consume and render that node recursively.\n\nIf these conditions hold, recursion is real rather than a special multi-document mode."
      },
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 0
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
